    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with the full suite green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned the identity key to `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and rewired duplicate/soft-match detection around it.\n\n**Files touched (5):**\n\n1. **`mapper/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained American Soundex utility (single `of` method, table-driven so its complexity stays low). Shared by the two consumers below.\n\n2. **`mapper/IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 `of(telephone, email)` \u2192 `of(telephone, email, lastName)`, now returning the 64-char SHA-256 hex over `telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)` (handles null email/telephone).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one-line mapping update to pass `owner.getLastName()`; the exposed `identityKey` field is now the hashed key.\n\n4. **`rest/function/owner/RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 two-line update so the 409 hard-duplicate check keys off the new identityKey (still skips soft-deleted owners; the disposable-email blocklist step already runs before it in the pipeline).\n\n5. **`rest/function/owner/DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft match now fires when `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` both match. Two owners with the same last name/postcode but different telephones therefore now get different keys and are created as a soft match rather than rejected.\n\nThe separate household-duplicate 409 (`RejectDuplicateHousehold` / `HouseholdId`) was already absent from the `owners.POST.yml` pipeline, so no removal was needed \u2014 duplicate detection is now the single identity key as the spec requires.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** each changed method stays simple (small CC, minimal changed lines), the shared Soundex logic lives in its own tiny class rather than bloating `IdentityKey`, and no large class was grown \u2014 the edits are 1\u20132 lines each except the deliberately-rewritten `DetectPossibleDuplicate.service`, which has no other methods to carry as context.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` both pass; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
